cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or its results, please cite the preprint below.
  The paper describes the design; this repository is the implementation and
  the measurements.
title: "Switchboard: an LLM model brokerage with policy-based routing and cross-model auditing"
abstract: >-
  Switchboard routes each task to the most efficient model under an explicit,
  versionable policy, then has a different model — preferably from a different
  provider — grade the output. Failed audits escalate one tier up carrying the
  auditor's findings; provider outages reroute on a separate budget; and every
  attempt is costed at observed token counts so the price of verification is
  visible rather than assumed. Zero runtime dependencies, stdlib only, and it
  runs fully offline against a mock provider.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Diaz Gutierrez de Quijano"
    given-names: "Joaquin"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-8354-1628"
repository-code: "https://github.com/JoaquinDG/switchboard"
license: MIT
version: "0.3.0"
date-released: "2026-08-15"
keywords:
  - large language models
  - model routing
  - cost optimization
  - cross-model auditing
  - LLM evaluation

